Zemya is dual-licensed, because its code and its data are not the same kind of thing.

  Code  — everything except content/ and public/data/     MIT      (below)
  Data  — content/ and public/data/                        ODbL-1.0 (below)

Why the data is ODbL: public/data/geography/countries.json is a derived database built
from world-countries (mledoze/countries), which is licensed ODbL-1.0, and ODbL is
share-alike, so the derived database has to be released under ODbL too.

Third-party datasets keep their own licences; see "Data sources" in README.md.


